degStats -- statistics on the degrees of a list of objects
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        degStats(List)
  * Inputs:
      * ideals, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of objects of type *note
        MonomialIdeal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, or any objects to which
        *note degree: (Macaulay2Doc)degree, can be applied.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note ShowTally: ShowTally, => ..., default value false, optional input
        to choose if the tally is to be returned
      * *note Verbose: degStats_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, optional input to request verbose feedback
  * Outputs:
      * a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, whose first entry is the
        average degree of a list of monomial ideals, second entry is the
        standard deviation of the degree, and third entry (if option turned on)
        is the degree tally

Description
===========

This function computes the degree of $R/I$ for each ideal $I$ in the list and
computes the mean and standard deviation of the degrees.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/101[a,b,c];                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : ideals = {monomialIdeal"a3,b,c2", monomialIdeal"a3,b,ac"}|
|                                                              |
|                      3      2                   3            |
|o2 = {monomialIdeal (a , b, c ), monomialIdeal (a , b, a*c)}  |
|                                                              |
|o2 : List                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : degStats(ideals)                                         |
|                                                              |
|o3 = (3.5, 2.5)                                               |
|                                                              |
|o3 : Sequence                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

The following examples use the existing functions *note randomMonomialSets:
randomMonomialSets, and *note idealsFromGeneratingSets:
idealsFromGeneratingSets, or *note randomMonomialIdeals: randomMonomialIdeals,
to automatically generate a list of ideals, rather than creating the list
manually:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ideals = idealsFromGeneratingSets(randomMonomialSets(4,3,1.0,3))        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {monomialIdeal (x , x , x , x ), monomialIdeal (x , x , x , x ),        |
|                      1   2   3   4                   1   2   3   4          |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     monomialIdeal (x , x , x , x )}                                         |
|                     1   2   3   4                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : degStats(ideals)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = (1, 0)                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : ideals = randomMonomialIdeals(4,3,1.0,3)                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {monomialIdeal (x , x , x , x ), monomialIdeal (x , x , x , x ),        |
|                      1   2   3   4                   1   2   3   4          |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     monomialIdeal (x , x , x , x )}                                         |
|                     1   2   3   4                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : degStats(ideals)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = (1, 0)                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that this function can be run with a list of any objects to which *note
degree: (Macaulay2Doc)degree, can be applied.

