dimStats -- statistics on the Krull dimension of a list of objects
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        dimStats(List)
  * Inputs:
      * ideals, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of objects of type *note
        MonomialIdeal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal, or any type to which *note
        dim: (Macaulay2Doc)dim, can be applied.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note ShowTally: ShowTally, => ..., default value false, optional input
        to choose if the tally is to be returned
      * *note Verbose: degStats_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, optional input to request verbose feedback
  * Outputs:
      * a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, whose first entry is the
        average Krull dimension of a list of monomial ideals, the second entry
        is the standard deviation of the Krull dimension, and third entry (if
        option turned on) is the Krull dimension tally

Description
===========

The function dimStats computes the average and standard deviation of the Krull
dimension for a list of monomial ideals.

