sample -- generates a sample from the given model
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        sample(Model,ZZ)
  * Inputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note Model: Model,, to be sampled from
      * N, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, sample size
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note Sample: Sample,, a sample of size $N$
        from the given model $M$

Description
===========

This function generates $N$ realizations of the random variable that has the
distribution specified by the given model.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : s=sample(ER(3,2,0.2),4)|
|                            |
|o1 = Sample{...4...}        |
|                            |
|o1 : Sample                 |
+----------------------------+

One obtains the data from the object of type *note Sample: Sample, (that is,
the actual sample in the statistical sense) as follows:

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : getData s                                                 |
|                                                               |
|            2   2     2           2         2               2  |
|o2 = {{x , x , x }, {x }, {x x , x , x x , x }, {x , x x , x }}|
|        3   2   3     2     1 3   2   2 3   3     1   1 2   2  |
|                                                               |
|o2 : List                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

The actual sample contains more information than just the data itself:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : peek s                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Sample{ModelName => Erdos-Renyi                                         |
|            Parameters => (3, 2, .2)                                         |
|            SampleSize => 4                                                  |
|                           2   2     2           2         2                 |
|            Data => {{x , x , x }, {x }, {x x , x , x x , x }, {x , x x ,    |
|                       3   2   3     2     1 3   2   2 3   3     1   1 2     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|    }                                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
| 2                                                                           |
|x }}                                                                         |
| 2                                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

and one can easily obtain sample statistics:

+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : statistics(s,degree@@ideal)          |
|                                          |
