File: RandomMonomialIdeals.info, Node: StdDev, Next: VariableName, Prev: statistics, Up: Top

StdDev -- a summary statistic for a list of objects
***************************************************

Description
===========

A sample standard deviation is -- along with sample mean -- one of the basic
summary statistics for a sample of randomly generated objects (or any list of
objects in general). The standard deviation value statistic for some property
of a list of objects is stored under the key StdDev in the hash table returned
by the function *note statistics: statistics,.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : s=sample(ER(6,3,0.2),100);             |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : myStats = statistics(s, degree@@ideal);|
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : myStats.StdDev                         |
|                                            |
|o3 = 5.113462623311135                      |
|                                            |
|o3 : RR (of precision 53)                   |
+--------------------------------------------+

The last line returns the standard deviation of the degrees of the 100 ideals
in the sample $s$. Note that it is more meaningful to look at this value along
with the mean value rather than as a stand-alone statistic.

See also
========

  * *note Mean: Mean, -- a summary statistic for a list of objects
  * *note statistics: statistics, -- generate statistics for a sample

For the programmer
==================

The object *note StdDev: StdDev, is a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

